# GROUND-TRUTH ASSET MANIFEST for server_rack_1..8
# Read with: pandas.read_csv(path, comment='#')
# Generated from the model.sdf files in this directory. If you edit a rack, edit this too.
# rack_model      : the <model name> that must NOT be renamed on <include> (the RfidReader
#                   <occluder><model> lookup is by plain name, RfidReader.cc:528).
#                   EXCEPTION: server_room.sdf renames on <include> to rack_rR_cC and names
#                   its occluders after THAT, which is equivalent and is why it works.
# tag_name        : the plain, unscoped model name RfidReader matches against <tag_prefix>
#                   and reports as detections[i].tagName. NOT the EPC. This is the only
#                   column that joins back to the SDF; 'equipment' is a type, not a link name.
# epc             : the CommsEndpoint <address>, used only by the RFComms read path.
#                   RfidReader is fully independent of it.
# z_local_m       : tag z in the RACK frame. World z = rack pose z + this.
# x_local_m       : tag x in the RACK frame, the tag COLUMN. +0.18 on racks 1-4, -0.18 on
#                   racks 5-8, measured as the viewer's right/left from the aisle (the face
#                   normal is local -Y, so an observer looks along +Y and local +X is their
#                   right). Racks 5-8 exist to break the single-column assumption that
#                   discovery_params.yaml tag_column still hard-codes; see Phase 5 of
#                   rfid_inventory_tracking/doc/versatility_roadmap.md.
#                   Tag y is always -0.503 (the tag is 4 mm thick, so it spans
#                   y = -0.505..-0.501, entirely in front of the -0.50 faceplate plane).
# Racks 5-8 carry the same equipment, U-map and z heights as 1-4 respectively; only the
# model name, tag prefix, EPC block and tag column differ.
# This file exists so the estimator can score non-detections against a manifest instead of
# against the reader's own <report_n_tags> count, which leaks the answer.
rack_model,tag_name,epc,equipment,u_start,u_end,u_size,depth_m,z_local_m,x_local_m
